  "bodyHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-family: arial;\"><span style=\"color: #0e101a;\"><br />Part1&gt; The Problem</span></span></p><p></p><div class=\"separator\" style=\"clear: both; text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEixGMdvpMbZCly_P6yKpCREnS9S349eaoyAEPpnRGX7rYz1a6JSewNkWg5a367EtXhvP8mL2XBxxAq_yPeIJyvc5o_CzIJrNfQGNzFolOERJ9mo8a1tBLuJh6PDEufBay-T7PoClDPkEQKuiH1BByXo76GuJry7vHjutdNMRnH4EPRGTi2yZIqa1ctw8A/s700/Time%20Travel.jpg\" style=\"clear: left; float: left; margin-bottom: 1em; margin-right: 1em;\"><img border=\"0\" data-original-height=\"525\" data-original-width=\"700\" height=\"78\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEixGMdvpMbZCly_P6yKpCREnS9S349eaoyAEPpnRGX7rYz1a6JSewNkWg5a367EtXhvP8mL2XBxxAq_yPeIJyvc5o_CzIJrNfQGNzFolOERJ9mo8a1tBLuJh6PDEufBay-T7PoClDPkEQKuiH1BByXo76GuJry7vHjutdNMRnH4EPRGTi2yZIqa1ctw8A/w105-h78/Time%20Travel.jpg\" width=\"105\" /></a></div><p></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\" style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\">It is my conjecture in the discussions of time travel that we might be forgetting to include space in it. We only know time through space example: a day is the rotation of Earth, and a year is the revolution of it around the Sun. Time alone is like describing&nbsp;</span><em style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\">nothingness</em><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\" style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\">.</span></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><br /></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\">Accordingly, our thought about time travel should be changed. It cannot work how the movies show us, we already have problems with that kind of time travel like the Grandfather's Paradox. Furthermore, I hypothesize another paradox, the Space Paradox, if I time travel 6 months back, I would land on the opposite side of the Solar System. I would be floating in space because Earth would have traveled 180 degrees around the Sun! To make it worse, all of this is possible only if we assume that our Solar System is stationary, else the Sun's motion can also be considered. Additionally, the Universe is expanding, and the Earth has gotten 27 seconds slower since 2016. To sum up, time is a very complex medium to travel in, I am not saying traveling back in time isn't possible, but it is not how we have thought of it till now!</p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><br /></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><br /></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><br /></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\" style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\">Part2&gt; The Solution</span></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><br /><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\" style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"></span></p><div class=\"separator\" style=\"clear: both; text-align: center;\"><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\" style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><a href=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjX2xYFofE3c4eQj1Cr46gmPKCN44WPgWHeK2tS9QtVWmKfGilXti4-NM-wdrES_BS_mObXcb3ISLQN8JXVDhlzBFT6rOQkMhHsR031miINYqM2IJLkcJRKBjfgGMaxV15Kl1zHeC53-PhmAYL2EXV7PyMx8E9hGdBQk8ZXbGznCGT1onJJbCVe2ntK5A/s1600/Teleportation.jpg\" style=\"clear: left; float: left; margin-bottom: 1em; margin-right: 1em;\"><img border=\"0\" data-original-height=\"900\" data-original-width=\"1600\" height=\"119\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjX2xYFofE3c4eQj1Cr46gmPKCN44WPgWHeK2tS9QtVWmKfGilXti4-NM-wdrES_BS_mObXcb3ISLQN8JXVDhlzBFT6rOQkMhHsR031miINYqM2IJLkcJRKBjfgGMaxV15Kl1zHeC53-PhmAYL2EXV7PyMx8E9hGdBQk8ZXbGznCGT1onJJbCVe2ntK5A/w130-h119/Teleportation.jpg\" width=\"130\" /></a></span></div><p></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><em style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\">\"In the middle of every difficulty lies an opportunity.\" ~Albert Einstein</em></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\" style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\">Following the steps of my favorite bald man, we should introspect into our daily lifestyle. Observing carefully, we seem to travel through space all the time! So, instead of time traveling through time, we do it through space.</span></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><br /></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><br /></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\" style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\">I am not crazy; I am just playing with what Einstein gave us: spacetime. Look at it this way, we are proceeding to a generation where science fiction merges with reality. Even today, I see articles about scientists discovering new particles that travel faster than light. If we want to travel back in time, we should focus on teleportation!</span></p><p style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; color: #0e101a; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\"><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\" style=\"background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-image: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-size: initial; margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt;\">If we could teleport onto a planet 3 light years away from Earth and point a high-end sci-fi telescope on Earth, we could see what happened 3 years from now! This way, we do not change the past yet can see it. No paradoxes emerge here, and instead of dreaming of the future, we take a step into making it real now!</span></p>",
  "summary": "An AS-level thought experiment arguing that any account of time travel must also track motion through space, then reframing observation of the past through distance and light.",
